\par }{\fs24 \tab Moon dogs can become ethereal and have the ability to travel in the ethereal and Astral plane at will. They have superior vision equal to double normal vision, including 60' infravisi
on. Combined with an unusually keen sense of smell and hearing, this grants moon dogs the detection abilities listed above, plus the ability to detect all illusions. Association with a moon dog for one hour or more removes }{\i\fs24 charms}{\fs24 
 and acts as a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24 .
\par \tab When in shadowy light, a moon dog is able to move in such a way as to effectively create magic equal to a }{\i\fs24 hypnotic pattern}{\fs24 
 of shadows. Only evil creatures will be affected. At the same time, each creature of good within the area will effectively gain a }{\i\fs24 protection from evil}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 remove fear}{\fs24 
 spell benefit. Moon dogs may not attack or perform any other action when weaving this pattern of shadows. It requires one full round to weave and extends to a range of 50 feet. The moon dog can }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24 , but doing s
o will force it back to its own plane immediately.
\par \tab Moon dogs may be damaged only by +2 or better magical weapons. They are never surprised (due to their keen senses) and cause opponents to subtract 3 from their surprise rolls. Moon dogs are immune to }{\i\fs24 fear}{\fs24 
 spells. They make all saving throws at a +2 bonus and takes half or quarter damage.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Habitat/Society:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Moon dogs are native to the plane of Elysium. They are champions of good and will often travel about the upper planes and the Prime Material plane to challenge evil.
\par \tab Moon dogs are friendly to all good and neutral races and those friendly to those races. They will not long associate with anyone because they are constantly on the move, hunting evil.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Ecology:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Moon dogs will often communicate with communities of men, using telepathy, in order to locate trouble spots among them.
\par 
