\par 
\par While not actively hostile, sapphire dragons are militantly territorial and initially distrustful of anyone who approaches.
\par    These beautiful dragons range from light to dark blue, and sparkle in the light, even at birth. Sapphire dragons are often mistaken for blue dragons, unless someone recalls the latter's preferred arid environment.
\par    Sapphire dragons speak their own tongue and the tongue common to all gem dragons, and 16% of hatchling sapphire dragons have an ability to communicate with any intellig
ent creature. The chance to possess this ability increases 5% per age category of the dragon.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Sapphire dragons generally observe intruders before deciding what to do with them, unless known enemies such as drow or dwarves are present. If others ar
e not actively hostile the dragon attempts conversation and spell use to determine their intentions and convince them to leave. If the dragon or its treasure is threatened, it attacks immediately with breath weapon, spells, and physical attacks. It uses p
sionics or other special abilities to escape if its life is in jeopardy.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Breath weapon/special abilities:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 This dragon's breath weapon is cone of high-pitched, almost inaudible sound, 75 feet long, 5 feet wide at the dragon's mouth, and 25 feet wide at the 
base. Creatures caught by the blast can save vs. breath weapon for half damage from the sound's disruption, and must make a second saving throw vs. breath weapon or be affected by fear, fleeing the dragon in panic for two rounds per age level of the drago
n, plus 1d6 rounds. This is a metabolic effect, and creatures unaffected by magical }{\i\fs24 fear}{\fs24 
 still suffer from the effects if they fail their save. Deafness does not protect one from the breath weapon's damage, though it prevents fear effects. A sapphire dragon casts spells and uses magical abilities at 7th level, plus combat modifier.
\par    Sapphire dragons are born with immunity to all forms of fear, as well as immunity to }{\i\fs24 web, hold, slow,}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 paralysis.}{\fs24  As they age, they gain the following additional powers: }{\b\fs24 Young:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 
continual light}{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Juvenile:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 stone shape}{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Adult:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 anti-magic shell}{\fs24  once a day. }{\b\fs24 Mature adult:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 passwall}{\fs24 
 six times a day. }{\b\fs24 Venerable:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 wall of stone}{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Great wyrm:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 sunray}{\fs24  three times a day.
\par 
