\par 
\par Gold dra
gons are wise, judicious, and benevolent. They often embark on self-appointed quests to promote goodness, and are not easily distracted from them. They hate injustice and foul play. A gold dragon frequently assumes human or animal guise and usually will b
e encountered disguised.
\par \tab At birth, a gold dragon's scales are dark yellow with golden metallic flecks. The flecks get larger as the dragon matures until, at the adult stage, the scales grow completely golden.
\par \tab Gold dragons speak their own tongue, a tongue common to all good dragons, and 18% of hatchling gold dragons have an ability to communicate with any intelligent creature. The chance to possess this ability increases 5% per age category of the dragon.

\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat: }{\fs24 Gold dragons usually parley before combat. When conversing with intelligent creatures they use }{\i\fs24 detect lie }{\fs24 and}{\i\fs24  detect gems}{\fs24  spells to gain the upper hand. In combat, they quickly use }{
\i\fs24 bless }{\fs24 and }{\i\fs24 luck bonus}{\fs24 . Older dragons use }{\i\fs24 luck bonus}{\fs24  at the start of each day if the duration is a day or more. They make heavy use of spells in combat. Among their favorites are}{\i\fs24 
 sleep, stinking cloud, slow, fire shield, cloudkill, globe of invulnerability, delayed blast fireball, }{\fs24 and}{\i\fs24  maze.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Breath weapon/special abilities: }{\fs24 A gold dragon has two breath weapons: a cone of }{\i\fs24 fire}{\fs24 
 90' long, 5' wide at the dragon's mouth, and 30' wide at the end or a cloud of potent chlorine gas 50' long, 40' wide and 30' high. Creatures caught in either effect are entitled to a save versus breath weapon for half damage.
\par \tab At birth, gold dragons have }{\i\fs24 water breathing}{\fs24  ability, can }{\i\fs24 speak with animals }{\fs24 freely, and are immune to fire and gas. They can also }{\i\fs24 polymorph self}{\fs24 
 three times a day. Each change form lasts until the dragon chooses a different form; reverting to the dragon's normal form does not co
unt as a change. A gold dragon's natural form has wings. However, they sometimes choose a wingless form to facilitate swimming, gaining the higher swimming rate listed above. A gold dragon in any wingless form can fly at a speed of 6 (MC E).
\par \tab As they age, they gain the following additional powers. }{\b\fs24 Young:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 bless}{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Juvenile:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 detect lie}{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Adult:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 
animal summoning}{\fs24  once a day. }{\b\fs24 Mature adult:}{\i\fs24  animal summoning }{\fs24 once a day. }{\b\fs24 Mature adult:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 luck bonus }{\fs24 once a day. }{\b\fs24 Old: }{\i\fs24 quest}{\fs24  once a day, and }{\i\fs24 
detect gems }{\fs24 three times a day. (This allows the dragon to know the number and kind of precious stones within a 30' radius, duration is one minute.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 luck bonus}{\fs24  power of mature adults is used to aid good adventurers. By touch the dragon can enchant one
 gem to bring good luck. The gem is usually one which has been embedded in the dragon's hide. When the dragon carries the gem, it and every good creature in a 10' radius per age category of the dragon receives a +1 bonus to all Saving Throws and similar d
ice rolls, cf. }{\i\fs24 stone of good luck}{\fs24 
. If the dragon gives a gem to another creature only the bearer gets the bonus. The enchantment lasts three hours per age category of the dragon. plus 1-3 hours. The enchantment ends if the gem is destroyed before its duration expires.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Habit/Society:}{\fs24\cf9 \tab  }{\fs24 
Gold dragons can live anywhere. Their lairs are secluded and always made of solid stone, either caves or castles. These usually have loyal guards: either animals appropriate to the terrain, or storm or good cloud giants. The gi
ants usually serve as guards through a mutual defensive agreement.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Ecology: }{\fs24 Gold dragons can eat almost anything, however, they usually sustain themselves on pearls or small gems. Gold dragons who receive pearls and gems from good or neutral creatures wil
