\par 
\par Silver dragons are kind and helpful. They will cheerfully assist good creatures if their need is genuine. They often take e the forms of kindly old men or fair damsels when associating with people.
\par \tab At birth, a silver dragon's scales are blue-gray with silver highlights. As the dragon approaches adulthood, 
its color slowly lightens to brightly gleaming silver. An adult or older silver dragon has scales so fine that the individual scales are scarcely visible. From a distance, these dragons look as if they have been sculpted from pure metal.
\par \tab Silver dragons sp
eak their own tongue, a tongue common to all good dragons, and 16% of hatchling silver dragons have an ability to communicate with any intelligent creature. The chance to possess this ability increases 5% per age category of the dragon.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat: }{\fs24 Silver dragons are not violent and avoid combat except when faced with highly evil or aggressive foes. If necessary, they use }{\i\fs24 feather fall}{\fs24  to stop any missiles fired at them. They use }{\i\fs24 wall of fog}{
\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 control weather}{\fs24  to blind or confuse opponents before making melee attacks. If angry, they will use }{\i\fs24 reverse gravity}{\fs24 
 to fling enemies helplessly into the air, where they can be snatched. When faced with flying opponents, a silver dragon will hide in clouds (often creating some with }{\i\fs24 control weather}{\fs24  on clear days), remain there using }{\i\fs24 
cloud walking}{\fs24 , then jump to the attack when they have the advantage.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Breath Weapon/Special Abilities: }{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 A silver dragon has two breath weapons: a cone of }{\i\fs24 cold}{\fs24  80' long, 5' wide at the dragon's mouth, and 30' wide at the end or a cloud of }{\i\fs24  paralyzation}{\fs24 
 gas 50' long, 40' wide, and 20' high. Creatures caught in the cold are allowed a save versus breath weapon for half damage. A silver dragon casts its spells and uses its magical abilities at 6th level, plus its combat modifier.
\par \tab At birth, silver dragons are immune to cold and can }{\i\fs24 polymorph self }{\fs24 three times a day. Each change in form lasts until the dragon chooses a different form and reverting to their normal form does not count as a change. They also can }
{\i\fs24 cloud walk}{\fs24 . This allows the dragon to tread on clouds or fog as though they were solid ground. The ability functions continuously, but can be negated or resumed at will. As they age, they gain the following additional powers: }{\b\fs24 
Young:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 feather fall}{\fs24  twice a day. }{\b\fs24 Juvenile:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 wall of fog}{\fs24  once a day. }{\b\fs24 Adult: }{\i\fs24 control winds}{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Mature adult:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 control weather}
{\fs24  once a day. }{\b\fs24 Old: }{\i\fs24  reverse gravity}{\fs24  once a day.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Habitat/Society: }{\fs24 Silver dragons prefer aerial lairs on secluded mountain peaks, or amid the clouds themselves. When they lair in clouds there always will be an enchanted area with a sold floor for laying eggs and storing treasure. 

\par \tab Silver dragons seem to prefer human form to their own, and often have mortal companions. Frequently they share deep friendships with mortals. Inevitab
ly, however, the dragon reveals its true form and takes its leave to live a dragon's life for a time.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Ecology: }{\fs24 Silver dragons prefer human food, and can live on such fare indefinitely.
\par \tab Because they lair in similar territories, silver dragons come into co
nflict with red dragons. Duels between the two species are furious and deadly, but silver dragons generally get the upper hand since they are more capable of working together against their foes and often have human allies.
\par 
