\par Juvenile\tab Cast }{\i\fs24 create water }{\fs24 once per day
\par Adult\tab Cast }{\i\fs24 sandstorm }{\fs24 (Mulhorandi spell) once per day
\par Venerable\tab Cast summon a 12-HD earth elemental
\par Great wyrm\tab Cast }{\i\fs24 disintegrate}{\fs24  once per day
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-1080\tx-720\tx720\tx1440\tx1800\tx2430\tx2790\tx3330\tx4680\tx5130\tx5310\tx6660\tx7470\tx7920\tx8640\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\adjustright {\fs24 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Habitat/Society:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Brown dragons are found in desert, often close to settled areas. They typically dwell in deep burrows nearly 1,000 feet beneath the sand, where they carve out vast chambers.
\par \tab The brown dragon mates and raises a family for only a short period of time; all parents encountered are in the mature adult stage of development. Many brown dragons do not mate.
\par \tab Man is the main enemy of brown dragons. Humans hunt for them for their hides and treasure. Blue dragons also attack brown dragons. 
\par \tab Battles between brown and blue dragons are legendary for their ferocity. The people of the desert have a curious respect for the brown dragon, so tales often make the blue dragons more evil than the brown.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Ecology: }{\fs24 Brown dragons are able to digest sand and other mineral materials to sustain themselves over long periods of time. However, meat is the preferred diet, with horseflesh a particular favorite.
\par 
