\par 
\par Cloud dragons are reclusive creatures that dislike intrusions. They rarely converse, but if persuaded to do so they tend to be taciturn and aloof. They have no respect whatsoever for creatures that cannot fly without assistance from spells or devices.

\par \tab A
t birth, cloud dragons have silver-white scales tinged with red at the edges. As they grow, the red spreads and lightens to sunset orange. At the mature adult stage and above, the red-orange color deepens to red gold and almost entirely replaces the silve
r.
\par \tab Cloud dragons speak their own tongue and a tongue common to all neutral dragons. Also 17% of hatchling cloud dragons can speak with any intelligent creature. The chance to possess this ability increases 5% per age category.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Cloud dragons are as likely to avoid combat (by assuming cloud form) as they are to attack. When attacking, they use their breath weapon to scatter foes, then cast }{\i\fs24 solid fog }{\fs24 
and use their manipulation abilities to blind and disorient their foes. When very angry, they conjure storms with }{\i\fs24 control weather}{\fs24  spells, then they call lightning. They like to use }{\i\fs24 stinking cloud }{\fs24 and }{\i\fs24 
control winds}{\fs24  spells against flying opponents.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Breath Weapon/Special Abilities:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 
A cloud dragon's breath weapon is an icy blast of air that is 140 feet long, 30 feet high, and 30 feet wide. Creatures caught in the blast suffer damage from cold and flying ice crystals. Furthermore, all creatures three size classes or more smaller than 
t
he dragon are blown head over heels for 2d12 feet, plus 3 feet per age category of the dragon. Characters who can grab solid objects won't be carried away unless they fail. Strength checks; creatures with claws, suction cups, etc., can avoid the effect if
 they have a suitable surface to cling to.
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-1080\tx-720\tx540\adjustright {\fs24 \tab A cloud dragon casts its spells and uses its magical abilities at 6th level plus its combat modifier.
\par \tab Cloud dragons are immune to cold.
\par \tab They can assume (or leave) a cohesive, cloud-like form at will, once per ro
und. In this form, they are 75% unlikely to be distinguished from normal clouds; when in cloud form, their Armor Class improves by -3 and their magic resistance increases by 15%. Cloud dragons can use their spells and innate abilities while in cloud form,
 but they cannot attack physically or use their breath weapon. In cloud form, cloud dragons fly at a speed of 12 (MC:A).
\par \tab As they age, cloud dragons gain the following additional powers. }{\b\fs24 Very young:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 solid fog}{\fs24  twice a day. }{\b\fs24 Young:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 stinking cloud}{\fs24  twice a day. }{\b\fs24 Juvenile:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 
creature water }{\fs24 twice a day (affects a maximum of three cubic yards [81 cubic feet]). }{\b\fs24 Adult:}{\fs24  }{\i\fs24 obscurement }{\fs24  three times a day. }{\b\fs24 Mature adult: }{\i\fs24 call lightning}{\fs24  twice a day. }{\b\fs24 Old:}{
\fs24  }{\i\fs24 weather summoning }{\fs24 twice a day. }{\b\fs24 Very old: }{\i\fs24 control weather}{\fs24  twice a day. }{\b\fs24 Ancient:}{\i\fs24  control winds}{\fs24  twice a day.
