\par 
\par Most small mammals are harmless to humans. Some have useful traits or abilities. Most animals have only rudimentary languages that humanoids cannot use except with the aid of magical spells. All have THAC0 20, except where noted below.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Beavers}{\fs24  quickly chew trees and construct homes in ponds. Adult pelts are worth two gp.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 House cats}{\fs24  are small, domesticated breeds.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Chipmunks}{\fs24  have excellent hearing and eyesight.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Ermines}{\fs24  are related to weasels. The white, spotted pelt is worth four gp.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Ferrets}{\fs24  are related to weasels. If captured as cubs or raised domestically, ferrets may be trained to perform simple tricks, retrieve objects, or hunt small burrowing game.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Foxes}{\fs24  have superb vision, hearing, and noses. Their pelts are worth three to five gp.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Gophers}{\fs24  live in large colonies burrowed into the soil of the plains. They have acute senses of hearing and smell. For each gopher encountered, another 1d10 are hiding in the burrows nearby.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Hedgehogs}{\fs24  are covered with sharp but harmless quills.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Moles}{\fs24  have an excellent ability to detect tastes and vibrations, but very poor vision.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Monkey}{\fs24  refers to a variety of small, non-hostile species (rhesus, spider, tamarind, lemurs, and others). THAC0 19.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Mice}{\fs24  infest virtually any human structure.
\par }{\b\fs24 \tab Minks}{\fs24  are related to weasels. The pelt is worth three gp.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Muskrats}{\fs24  have a moderately valuable pelt worth five sp.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Opossum}{\fs24  are woodland marsupials with good hearing.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Otters}{\fs24  are fast runners (12) and swimmers (18). They are friendly and only attack if cornered or if their young are threa
tened. Pelts are worth two to three gp. Giant otters are identical except for their size (10'-15' long). Pelts are worth 1,000-4,000 gp. THAC0 19 (sea and giant otters).
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Pigs}{\fs24  may bite or attempt to stun, then crush a victim by butting. Domestic pigs are n
ormally harmless unless angered or magically controlled. Wild pigs are domestic pigs that have escaped to the wild. They are smaller (2 feet long) and nonaggressive unless provoked. THAC0 19.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Rabbits}{\fs24  are difficult to surprise or catch due to their sensitive eyesight, hearing, nose, and natural paranoia.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Raccoons}{\fs24  only attack if cornered or rabid (10% chance). The pelts are worth one gp.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Squirrels}{\fs24  have good vision and hearing.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Flying squirrels}{\fs24  have furry membranes that enable them to glide five feet for each one foot they drop.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Giant black squirrels}{\fs24  are 2-foot-long residents of evil-dominated forests. They steal loose, small valuables (rings, gems, vials) to decorate their nests. THAC0 19.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Woodchucks}{\fs24  are capable of quickly gnawing through trees or wood. The pelts are worth 1 gp.
\par   
