\par 
\par Quaggoths are humanoids with long, shaggy, white hair covering their entire bodies. They wear no clothing. Warlike and vicious, they roam the Underdark looking for prey. Drow sometimes enslave them as guards and spider handlers.
\par \tab Quaggoths speak a halting form of Undercommon, and can grasp only simple concepts. More intelligent quaggoths may also speak a few words of Duergar, Drow, or Common.
\par \tab These aggressive beasts have infravision with a range of 120'. They are immune to all poisons.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Quaggoth tribes claim a certain territory as theirs and patrol it, hunting for food. Any detected animals or creatures (such as a party of adventurers) invite certain attack.
\par \tab Most tribes (70%) of quaggoths do not 
carry weapons, and attack with their claws for 1-4 hit points of damage per hit. The remainder of quaggoth tribes carry stone clubs or axes. Those quaggoths which are or have been drow slaves carry superior weapons, such as steel battle axes or two-handed
 swords.
\par \tab If a quaggoth is reduced to 25% or less of its original hit points, it enters a berserk fury and receives a +2 bonus to its attack and damage rolls. This rage lasts until the quaggoth dies or all enemies are dead or out of sight.
\par \tab For every 12 qua
ggoths encountered, there will be a leader, or jald. The jald has 3+3 Hit Dice and wears leather or skins, making it AC 5. In addition, it gains a +1 bonus to damage rolls. Jalds direct combat; if no jald is present, the quaggoths will fall upon their pre
y, whatever it is, in an unorganized manner
\par \tab Any quaggoth tribe has a 20% chance of having one or two thonots. A thonot is the quaggoth equivalent of a shaman. Instead of magic, however, thonots use psionics. A thonot will use its abilities to aid the tribe in combat, escape, or healing.
\par \tab If quaggoths win combat, they take all bodies, including those of dead quaggoths, to their lair and devour them.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-1080\tx1440\tx2880\tx5040\tx6480\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf9 Psionics Summary}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 (Thonots only):
