\par 
\par Tritons are rumored to be creatures from the elemental plane of Water that have been placed on the Prime Material plane for some purpose unknown to m
an. They are sea dwellers, inhabiting warmer waters principally but equally able to live at shallow or great depths.
\par \tab The lower half of a triton ends in two finned legs, while its torso, head, and arms are handsomely human
. Tritons have a silvery skin that fades into silver-blue scales on the lower half of their bodies. Their hair is deep blue or blue-green. Triton speak their own language as well as those of sea elves and locathah.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Tritons carry either tridents (60%) or long spears (40%). Some 25% are also armed with heavy crossbows. When equipped for battle, tritons wear armor made of scales (AC 4).
\par \tab Outside their lair, tritons are 90% likely to be mounted, either on hippocampi (65%) or giant sea horses (35%). These mounts fight in defense of their riders.
\par \tab Exceptional tritons (see below) and triton leaders always carry conch shells with them. Not magical, their sounds are well known to all marine creatures. When blown properly by an exceptional triton, a conch sum
mons 5d4 hippocampi, 1d10 sea lions, or 5d6 giant sea horses. These creatures swim to the aid of the summoning triton, arriving 1d6 rounds after the conch is first sounded. The conchs can also be sounded to frighten aquatic animals as the }{\i\fs24 fear}{
\fs24  spell. This 
latter noise causes all marine creatures within 60 feet and with animal Intelligence or less to flee in panic. Creatures are allowed a saving throw vs. spell to avoid the fear effect, but even those who succeed with their saving throws have a -5 modifier 
on their attack rolls against the tritons.
\par \tab Triton are reclusive and nonviolent. They normally attack to capture. If a triton is killed in a battle, however, the fight immediately becomes one of retribution. Should the fighting go poorly, the tritons withdr
aw to their lair to either gather reinforcements or make a last stand.
\par \tab In addition to their other abilities, tritons are nearly impervious to magic with a natural magic resistance of 90%.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Habitat/Society:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Tritons live either in great undersea castles (80
% chance) or in finely sculpted caverns (20%). While tritons lean toward good alignment, they are very suspicious of outsiders and have no love for land dwellers in general.
\par \tab Tritons rarely kill, unless provoked, but they are quick to apprehend those who i
ntrude upon their seas. Trespassers found guilty of intentionally entering triton waters or treasure seeking are left ``to the fate of the seas.'' This means being stripped of all belongings and set adrift at least 10 miles from any shoreline. Characters 
ruled innocent by the triton court awaken the next day on some distant shore. Tritons never aid land dwellers unless their own interests are involved in the matter.
\par \tab For every 10 tritons encountered there is an exceptional triton of 4-6 Hit Dice. For every 
20 encountered there is an exceptional triton with 7-8 Hit Dice. Groups of 50 or more are always accompanied by a triton leader (AC 2, 9 Hit Dice). There is a 10% chance for every 10 tritons encountered that they are accompanied by a triton mage of 1d6 le
vels.
\par \tab At a triton lair, the following additional tritons are always found:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-1080\adjustright {\fs24 60 males (with related exceptional tritons)
\par One mage of 7th- to 10th-level ability
\par One priest of 8th- to 11th-level ability
\par Four priests of 2nd- to 5th-level ability
\par Female tritons equal to 100% of males (2 HD, AC 6)
\par Young equal to 100% of males (noncombatants)
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-1080\tx180\tx1170\tx1620\tx2070\tx2520\tx3330\tx4320\tx5400\tx5940\tx6660\tx7740\tx8100\tx9450\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\adjustright {\fs24 
\par There is also a 75% chance that the lair contains 2d6 sea lions as pets/guards.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Ecology:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Tritons are omnivorous and live on fish, shellfish, and sea weed. They have no natu
ral enemies save the giant squid, which is immune to the effects of their conch shells. Normal triton live approximately 300 years while their leaders and spellcasters have life expectancies of 500 years or more.
\par   
\par 
