\par 
\par These yugoloths are summoned by evil wizards or priests to guard something of importance. Yugoloth guardians always defend their charge with great ferocity.
\par \tab There are three types of yugoloth guardians -- least, lesser, and 
greater. The least and lesser yugoloth guardians vary in size and form, often being horned and frog-like (least) or ape- or boar-like (lesser). Greater yugoloth guardians always appear as gigantic, winged bears with ram horns protruding from their forehea
ds, and eagle talons for hands.
\par \tab yugoloths guardian have the ability to speak all languages.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Combat:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 yugoloth guardians can breath fire three times per day in a cone 30 feet long with a 10-foot base diameter. Damage depends upon the type of daemon breathin
g. Least and lesser yugoloths cause 3d6 and 5d6 points of damage, respectively, while greater yugoloths inflict 7d6 points per breath attack. A successful saving throw vs. breath weapon reduces damage by half. Yugoloth guardians never use their fire breat
h if the fire might damage whatever they are assigned to protect.
\par \tab All yugoloth guardians are immune to }{\i\fs24 charm, hold, sleep, polymorph}{\fs24 , and }{\i\fs24 fear}{\fs24  spells. Lesser and greater yugoloths are also impervious to weapons with less than a +2 bonus. Many of these crea
tures are invulnerable to one or more additional forms of attack (e.g., sword, cold, fire, electricity).
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Habitat/Society:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Yugoloth guardians must remain at all times within 90 yards of the object they have been summoned to protect. Within this 90-yard rad
ius, yugoloth guardians prefer to remain at a distance in battle, using their breath weapon to maximum advantage.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Ecology:}{\fs24\cf9  }{\fs24 Summoning a guardian daemon is a dangerous affair. There is a 10% chance for each level the summoner is over 7th level of having his
 request for a guardian daemon granted (maximum chance of 90%). Conversely, if the summoning fails, there is a 30% chance (-2% per level of the summoner over 10th) that the daemon takes offense and gates in to slay the spellcaster.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Least Yugoloth
\par }{\fs24 These creatures are often summoned to protect treasures valued at less than 25,000 gold pieces. Least yugoloths have a 50% chance of being immune to one additional type of attack.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Lesser Yugoloth
\par }{\fs24 Lesser yugoloths are usually found guarding treasures of 25,000 gold pieces or more. They have a 80% chance of being impervious to one additional attack form.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf9 Greater Yugoloth
\par }{\fs24 These yugoloths are dispatched only to protect objects of exceedingly great value. Greater yugoloth guardians are resistant to magic (25%) and are always immune to two additional forms of attack. They can make a }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24 
, as the spell, once per round, even when engaged in combat.
\par   
\par 
